# XCU cksum
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# All tests run in the POSIX locale. The expected values are the CRC and
# octet count the page's algorithm gives for each input.

assertion  XCU.cksum.001
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       cksum writes the CRC (as an unsigned number) and the octet count for fixed inputs, with the length included in the CRC.
test       t/001-known-values.sh

assertion  XCU.cksum.002
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#INPUT FILES
class      required
since      1992
says       Bytes of every value, including NUL, and lengths that take more than one octet to record, give the defined CRC.
test       t/002-binary-and-long.sh

assertion  XCU.cksum.003
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#OPERANDS/file
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#STDIN
class      required
since      1992
says       Each file operand gives a line of checksum, octet count and pathname, in order; with no operand the line has no pathname and no leading space.
test       t/003-operands-and-format.sh

assertion  XCU.cksum.004
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/cksum.html#STDERR
class      required
since      1992
says       A file that cannot be read gives a diagnostic and a nonzero status and no result line; success gives 0.
test       t/004-errors.sh
